{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I am one hundred and twenty years old today; I can no longer go out and come in.</b> For I have grown old, and also because HaShem said to me: You shall not cross the Jordan, etc. And you — you have no loss in this, for HaShem your Elohim, He is the one who crosses before you, and you have none like Him. Another interpretation: I can no longer go out and come in — not because of weakness, but because HaShem said to me: You shall not cross, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:34.462830410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}